From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mike Jackson (EDGE)" <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:31:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] Exclude date/time autofill preview text from copy and
 drag

While an Autofill suggestion is previewed, date, month, week, time and
datetime-local inputs render the would-be value as text in their UA
shadow tree. That text was selectable so copy, cut and selection drags
serialized it into text/plain, letting a page read previewed data, such
as a stored card's expiration date, from dragstart before the user
accepted the suggestion. Make the previewed date/time pseudo-elements
unselectable and read-only in the UA stylesheet, matching the <select>
and text control previews. Accepted autofilled values are still copied.

Bug: 578051925
Change-Id: Id5459fc6452c43f80f3ef6609a544511170983ed
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8669079
Reviewed-by: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mike Jackson <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728692}
(cherry picked from commit 0441415b72b922e1c14ad3320fd230d1608ea651)
